#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""review-intent: print the "Owner intent" block for a reviewer brief, from the ledger, verbatim.

usage: review-intent [--pr OWNER/REPO#N | --pr REPO#N] [--body-file F ...] [--ask N ...] [--decision N ...] [--state-dir DIR] [--skip-record-check]

A reviewer judges a change against the owner's words, not against a lead's restatement of them (findings-contract.md, "The owner-intent block").
This script collects the ledger ids a change cites and prints one markdown block that quotes each ask and decision exactly, so the driver appends it to the
round's brief.md:   review-intent --pr cartwmic/coordinator#782 >> round-1/brief.md   (add --body-file round-1/brief.md when the brief itself cites ids)

Inputs: the PR's agent record (--pr; the file <traces dir>/emitted/review/<repo>#N/pr-record.md when it exists), else the PR body (--pr, read with gh); any text files
(--body-file, repeatable); and ids given by hand. When the record is used, the decisions the ledger links to that PR (a live decision whose `pr` is that PR) are collected too, because the record is no longer
where `ledger pr-decisions-check` has them listed; the body path is unchanged.
The traces dir is $AGENT_TRACES_DIR, else ~/.local/share/agent-traces. Read-only: it reads the ledger and prints.
What it collects (the grammar is in findings-contract.md; agent-traces review add applies the same one to the brief):
  every #N on a `Decisions:` line (decisions); every `ask #N` / `asks #N` (with `#N-#M` ranges and `, #M` lists), asks;
  for a PR that touches `leads/<type>.*`, the ask ids in `approved_by` of `leads/<type>.json` at the PR head (when the file has the key; --pr only);
  the ask each collected decision names (its ask_id, and any `ask #N` in its why); and for each collected ask, the ask its workstream's creation why cites.
An id the ledger does not know is an error (exit 1, each id named): fix the citation, do not drop it. (The one exception: a number found only in a workstream's free-text
creation why, where `ask 870` needs no `#`, is left out if no such ask exists.)
For each ask the block also quotes what he wrote in the Other box after answering (his follow-ups), which `ledger show --json` leaves out: they are read from `ledger show ask N --history`.
Record check (--pr only): before anything is read, the PR's agent record is checked with `pr-body-check OWNER/REPO N --skip-intent-review` (the merge check, minus the review
that has not happened yet). The run is refused (exit 3, nothing on stdout, pr-body-check's own output on stderr) when that check reports a record defect: no record, no complete
principles table, no Decisions line, or a Decisions line the ledger does not match. Fix the record, then build the brief. A round is not spent on what a tool already finds.
Only record defects refuse. The check's other findings (ids or bookkeeping in the description, a Proven section that misses the head, a red or running head run) are printed as a
note and do not stop the run: a review can still find them useful to see, and some cannot pass until the review is done. If `pr-body-check` is not on PATH (the work profile has none),
cannot reach GitHub or the ledger, or times out, the run goes on with a warning: a broken tool never blocks a review. --skip-record-check turns the check off.
Merge check (--pr only): after the record check, the repo's own merge script is run in its check-only mode, `scripts/merge-pr.sh N --check-only`, which runs every check the real merge runs except the
review round (and the main-run state, which is not a defect of the PR) and merges nothing. The coordinator's and the homelab's merge scripts have it (agent-kit, loop-engine and dotfiles have no merge script of their own:
they merge through pr-body-check, which the record check covers). The script is found at <checkouts>/<repo name>/scripts/merge-pr.sh, where <checkouts> is $REVIEW_INTENT_CHECKOUTS, else ~/git: the checkout the
repo's pr-body-check already runs from. The run is refused (exit 3, nothing on stdout) when the script exits 1 and says REFUSED: its whole output goes to stderr, then a line saying to fix it before building the
brief. This goes further than the record check: a red or still-running head run, a Proven section that misses the head, bookkeeping in the description, a missing gate run or RECORD or RED line all refuse here, because the
merge would refuse them. A script that is not there (a checkout that cannot be found, the work profile), is too old to know the flag (exit 64), exits any other way, or runs over MERGE_CHECK_SECONDS is a warning
and the run goes on, as for the record check. --skip-record-check turns both checks off.
Exit 0 the block is printed; 1 an id is unknown; 2 bad arguments, no ledger, or gh failed; 3 the PR's agent record fails pr-body-check, or the repo's merge script refuses it before the review.
Log: every run appends one JSON line to $XDG_STATE_HOME/review-intent/log.jsonl (else ~/.local/state/review-intent/log.jsonl), written at the one place main() returns, so a
refusal added later is recorded without more code. Fields: ts, tool ("review-intent"), pr (the --pr value or ""), outcome (done: exit 0; refused: exit 1 or 3; failed: exit 2),
exit, reason (the first line the run printed to stderr, or ""), record_check (passed, refused, skipped-flag, fail-open-missing, fail-open-error, fail-open-timeout, not-run: no --pr),
merge_check (the same values, for the repo's merge script), duration_ms.
A log line that cannot be written never changes the exit code.

The block (one per brief):
    ## Owner intent (generated by review-intent)
    <!-- review-intent v1 asks=<ids|none> decisions=<ids|none> sha256=<hex of the body> -->
    <body: every line between this marker line and the end marker, each ending in a newline>
    <!-- /review-intent -->
The sha256 is of the body's UTF-8 bytes (LF line ends). Nothing time-dependent is in the body, so the same ledger gives the same sha.
The ledger is $COORDINATOR_STATE_DIR, else ~/.local/share/coordinator, else ~/.local/share/coordinator-work (the work Mac); --state-dir wins.
"""
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import time

HEADER = "## Owner intent (generated by review-intent)"
END = "<!-- /review-intent -->"
INTRO = (
    "The owner's own words are quoted below from the ledger, exactly as recorded. Judge the change against them ahead of any restated intent in this brief. "
    "A guarantee quoted here that the change does not keep is a finding, even when the restated intent does not mention it."
)
NONE_LINE = "No ask or decision is cited by this change: judge it on the principles and the restated intent only, and say that no owner approval is cited."

DASHES = "-–—"
ITEM = r"#(\d+)(?:\s*[%s]\s*#?(\d+))?" % DASHES
ASK_LIST = re.compile(r"\basks?\s+(%s(?:\s*(?:,|and|&)\s*%s)*)" % (ITEM, ITEM), re.I)
ITEM_RE = re.compile(ITEM)
# A workstream's creation why is free text a person or agent wrote ("Michael's Other answer on ask 870"), so there the `#` is optional.
# Only the first item of a list may leave it out ("ask 870", "asks 1113-1115"); a later item needs it ("ask #1175, 22:09Z" is one ask and a time).
# A `#N` is always an id, unless a digit or a time follows ("#5:30"); a bare N is not when a time or a unit follows ("ask 5 minutes", "ask 5pm", "ask 3 times").
UNITS = r"(?:seconds?|secs?|minutes?|mins?|hours?|hrs?|days?|weeks?|months?|years?|times?)"
RANGE_END = r"(?:\s*[%s]\s*#?(\d+))?" % DASHES
LOOSE_FIRST = r"(?:#(\d+)(?!\d|:\d)%s|(\d+)(?!\d|:|\s*%s\b|\s*[ap]m\b|[hms]\b)%s)" % (RANGE_END, UNITS, RANGE_END)
LOOSE_LIST = re.compile(r"\basks?\s+(%s(?:\s*(?:,|and|&)\s*%s)*)" % (LOOSE_FIRST, ITEM), re.I)
LOOSE_ITEM_RE = re.compile(r"(?:%s)|(?:%s)" % (LOOSE_FIRST, ITEM))


class Usage(Exception):
    pass


class RecordRefused(Exception):
    pass


class MergeRefused(Exception):
    pass


def line_ids(text, label):
    """The ids (#N) on every `label:` line, bold and italic marks ignored (the way pr-body-check reads `Decisions:`)."""
    found = []
    for line in text.splitlines():
        rest = re.match(r"^%s:(.*)$" % re.escape(label), line.replace("*", "").replace("_", "").strip(), re.I)
        if rest:
            found += [int(n) for n in re.findall(r"#(\d+)", rest.group(1))]
    return found


def ask_refs(text, loose=False):
    """The ids in `ask #N`, `asks #N-#M`, `asks #N, #M and #K` (with `loose`, the `#` may be left out: `ask 870`)."""
    found = []
    for m in (LOOSE_LIST if loose else ASK_LIST).finditer(text):
        for groups in (LOOSE_ITEM_RE if loose else ITEM_RE).findall(m.group(1)):
            a, b = next((groups[i], groups[i + 1]) for i in range(0, len(groups), 2) if groups[i])
            lo = int(a)
            hi = int(b) if b else lo
            found += list(range(lo, hi + 1)) if hi >= lo else [lo]
    return found


def without_block(text):
    """The text with any earlier generated block cut out, so its ids are not read as citations."""
    return re.sub(r"^%s\n.*?^%s[ \t]*\n?" % (re.escape(HEADER), re.escape(END)), "", text, flags=re.M | re.S)


def quote(text):
    return "\n".join("> " + l if l else ">" for l in str(text).replace("\r\n", "\n").split("\n"))


class Ledger:
    def __init__(self, state_dir):
        self.state = state_dir
        self.bin = os.path.join(state_dir, "pane-bin", "ledger")
        if not os.access(self.bin, os.X_OK):
            raise Usage("review-intent: no ledger at %s (set COORDINATOR_STATE_DIR or pass --state-dir)" % self.bin)

    def show(self, kind, key):
        env = dict(os.environ, COORDINATOR_STATE_DIR=self.state)
        p = subprocess.run([self.bin, "show", kind, str(key), "--json"], env=env, capture_output=True, text=True)
        if p.returncode != 0:
            return None
        try:
            return json.loads(p.stdout)
        except ValueError:
            return None


    def decisions_for_pr(self, repo, n):
        """The ids of the live decisions the ledger links to the PR (`decisions.pr`, compared without regard to case, as GitHub does). A ledger that cannot list them is an error: a linked decision must not drop out because a call failed."""
        env = dict(os.environ, COORDINATOR_STATE_DIR=self.state)
        p = subprocess.run([self.bin, "list", "decisions", "--json"], env=env, capture_output=True, text=True)
        try:
            if p.returncode != 0:
                raise ValueError(p.stderr.strip())
            rows = json.loads(p.stdout)
        except ValueError as e:
            raise Usage("review-intent: the ledger could not list decisions (needed for the PR's linked decisions): %s" % e)
        want = ("%s#%s" % (repo, n)).lower()
        return sorted(r["id"] for r in rows if isinstance(r, dict) and not r.get("voided_at") and str(r.get("pr") or "").lower() == want)

    def follow_ups(self, n):
        """What he wrote in the Other box while the ask was open, oldest first, as (time, text). `show --json` leaves these out; `show ask N --history` prints
        each as `  follow-up <time> by <who>: <text>` (text may run over several lines) among the other lines that start with two spaces and a word."""
        env = dict(os.environ, COORDINATOR_STATE_DIR=self.state)
        p = subprocess.run([self.bin, "show", "ask", str(n), "--history"], env=env, capture_output=True, text=True)
        if p.returncode != 0:
            return []
        header = re.compile(r"^  (?:follow-up|reply|revised|by|last changed by|with|closed by|answered at|answer|evidence|recommend|question|\d+\)) ")
        found, current = [], None
        for line in p.stdout.split("\n"):
            m = re.match(r"^  follow-up (\S+) by ([^:]*): ?(.*)$", line)
            if m:
                current = [m.group(1), m.group(3), m.group(2)]
                found.append(current)
            elif header.match(line) or line.startswith("#"):
                current = None  # another line of the ask's record: the follow-up's text is over
            elif current is not None:
                current[1] += "\n" + line
        return [(t, text.rstrip("\n"), who) for t, text, who in found]


def default_state_dir():
    home = os.path.expanduser("~")
    given = os.environ.get("COORDINATOR_STATE_DIR")
    if given:
        return given
    for name in ("coordinator", "coordinator-work"):
        d = os.path.join(home, ".local/share", name)
        if os.access(os.path.join(d, "pane-bin", "ledger"), os.X_OK):
            return d
    return os.path.join(home, ".local/share/coordinator")


def gh(args, what):
    p = subprocess.run(["gh", *args], env=dict(os.environ, GH_CALLER="review-intent"), capture_output=True, text=True)
    if p.returncode != 0:
        raise Usage("review-intent: gh could not read %s: %s" % (what, p.stderr.strip()))
    return p.stdout


def pr_ref(spec):
    m = re.match(r"^(?:([\w.-]+)/)?([\w.-]+)#(\d+)$", spec)
    if not m:
        raise Usage("review-intent: --pr takes OWNER/REPO#N (or REPO#N for cartwmic/REPO), got %r" % spec)
    return "%s/%s" % (m.group(1) or "cartwmic", m.group(2)), m.group(3)


def record_path(spec):
    """Where the PR's agent record lives: <traces dir>/emitted/review/<repo>#N/pr-record.md, next to the review rounds (the same item name they use)."""
    repo, n = pr_ref(spec)
    root = os.environ.get("AGENT_TRACES_DIR") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".local/share/agent-traces")
    return os.path.join(root, "emitted", "review", "%s#%s" % (repo.split("/")[1], n), "pr-record.md")


def pr_text(spec):
    """(text, from_record): the PR's agent record when there is one, else its body."""
    path = record_path(spec)
    if os.path.isfile(path):
        try:
            with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                return fh.read(), True
        except OSError as e:
            raise Usage("review-intent: cannot read %s: %s" % (path, e.strerror))
    return pr_body(spec), False


def pr_body(spec):
    repo, n = pr_ref(spec)
    return gh(["pr", "view", n, "--repo", repo, "--json", "body", "--jq", ".body"], "%s#%s" % (repo, n))


LEADS_FILE = re.compile(r"^leads/([\w-]+)\.[A-Za-z]+$")


def pr_approvals(spec):
    """For a PR that touches `leads/<type>.*`: [(type, [ask ids])] from `approved_by` in `leads/<type>.json` at the PR head. A type with no such file at the head (gh says 404), or no usable key, is
    skipped; any other gh failure is an error (a founding ask must not drop out because a call failed)."""
    repo, n = pr_ref(spec)
    what = "%s#%s" % (repo, n)
    head = gh(["pr", "view", n, "--repo", repo, "--json", "headRefOid", "--jq", ".headRefOid"], what).strip()
    names = gh(["api", "--paginate", "repos/%s/pulls/%s/files" % (repo, n), "--jq", ".[].filename"], what + " (its files)").split("\n")  # every file, not the first page
    types = sorted({m.group(1) for name in names for m in [LEADS_FILE.match(name.strip())] if m})
    found = []
    for t in types:
        p = subprocess.run(["gh", "api", "-H", "Accept: application/vnd.github.raw+json", "repos/%s/contents/leads/%s.json?ref=%s" % (repo, t, head)],
                           env=dict(os.environ, GH_CALLER="review-intent"), capture_output=True, text=True)
        if p.returncode != 0:
            if "404" in p.stderr:
                continue  # the PR has no leads/<type>.json at its head (a README, or a deleted type)
            raise Usage("review-intent: gh could not read leads/%s.json at %s of %s: %s" % (t, head[:8], what, p.stderr.strip()))
        try:
            ids = json.loads(p.stdout).get("approved_by")
        except (ValueError, AttributeError):
            continue
        if isinstance(ids, list) and ids and all(isinstance(i, int) and not isinstance(i, bool) and i > 0 for i in ids):
            found.append((t, sorted(set(ids))))
    return found


def option_line(options, n):
    if not isinstance(n, int) or not options or not 1 <= n <= len(options):
        return None
    o = options[n - 1]
    if isinstance(o, dict):
        return "%d) %s: %s" % (n, o.get("title", ""), o.get("consequence", "")) if o.get("consequence") else "%d) %s" % (n, o.get("title", ""))
    return "%d) %s" % (n, o)


def labelled(label, text):
    """`Label: text` for one line, else the label and the text quoted: no line of ledger text can then look like a line of the block's own (the end marker)."""
    text = str(text).replace("\r\n", "\n")
    return "%s: %s" % (label, text) if "\n" not in text else "%s:\n%s" % (label, quote(text))


def render_ask(a, why, follow_ups):
    out = ["### Ask #%d" % a["id"], "Cited because: %s" % "; ".join(sorted(why))]
    if a.get("workstream"):
        out.append("Workstream: %s" % a["workstream"])
    out.append("Answered: %s" % (a.get("answered_at") or "not answered"))
    out += ["Summary:", quote(a.get("summary") or ""), labelled("Question", a.get("question") or "(none)")]
    pick = option_line(a.get("options"), a.get("answer_choice"))
    out.append(labelled("Chosen option", pick or "none picked"))
    said = False
    for field, label in (("answer", "His answer (verbatim)"), ("answer_other", "His own words when no option fit (verbatim)")):
        if a.get(field):
            out += ["%s:" % label, quote(a[field])]
            said = True
    for at, text, who in follow_ups:
        if text in (a.get("answer"), a.get("answer_other")):
            continue  # the ledger also files an "Other" answer as a follow-up: it is already quoted above
        mine = who.lower().startswith("michael")
        out += ["%s, written %s while the ask was open (verbatim):" % ("His follow-up" if mine else "Follow-up by %s" % who, at), quote(text)]
        said = True
    if not said:
        out.append("His words: none recorded; he picked the option only.")
    return "\n".join(out)


def render_decision(d, why):
    out = ["### Decision #%d" % d["id"], "Cited because: %s" % "; ".join(sorted(why))]
    if d.get("voided_at"):
        out.append("Voided: %s" % (d.get("voided_why") or "yes"))
    out += [labelled("Summary", d.get("summary", "")), labelled("Question", d.get("question") or "(none)")]
    chosen = option_line(d.get("options"), d.get("chose"))
    out.append(labelled("Chosen option", chosen or "none recorded"))
    out.append(labelled("Why", d.get("why") or "(none)"))
    out.append("Ask: %s" % ("#%d" % d["ask_id"] if d.get("ask_id") else "none"))
    return "\n".join(out)


def build(texts, asks_given, decisions_given, ledger, approvals=(), linked=()):
    """Returns (block, errors). `texts` are the PR body and body files; each id keeps the reasons it was collected for."""
    ask_why, dec_why = {}, {}

    def add(table, n, reason):
        table.setdefault(n, set()).add(reason)

    for n in asks_given:
        add(ask_why, n, "--ask")
    for n in decisions_given:
        add(dec_why, n, "--decision")
    for n in linked:
        add(dec_why, n, "the ledger links it to this PR")
    for t, ids in approvals:
        for n in ids:
            add(ask_why, n, "approved_by of the lead type %s (leads/%s.json at the PR head)" % (t, t))
    for t in texts:
        t = without_block(t)
        for n in line_ids(t, "Decisions"):
            add(dec_why, n, "a Decisions: line")
        for n in ask_refs(t):
            add(ask_why, n, "named in the text")
    errors, decisions, asks = [], {}, {}
    for n in sorted(dec_why):
        d = ledger.show("decision", n)
        if d is None:
            errors.append("decision #%d is not in the ledger at %s" % (n, ledger.state))
            continue
        decisions[n] = d
        if d.get("ask_id"):
            add(ask_why, d["ask_id"], "ask of decision #%d" % n)
        for m in ask_refs(d.get("why") or ""):
            add(ask_why, m, "named in the why of decision #%d" % n)
    cited = sorted(ask_why)
    for n in cited:
        a = ledger.show("ask", n)
        if a is None:
            errors.append("ask #%d is not in the ledger at %s" % (n, ledger.state))
            continue
        asks[n] = a
    for n in cited:  # one hop: the ask that opened the cited ask's workstream; the asks found this way are not followed again
        a = asks.get(n)
        w = ledger.show("workstream", a["workstream"]) if a and a.get("workstream") else None
        for m in ask_refs((w or {}).get("why") or "", loose=True):
            if m != n:
                add(ask_why, m, "opened the workstream %s of ask #%d" % (json.dumps(a["workstream"]), n))
    for n in sorted(set(ask_why) - set(asks)):
        if n in cited:
            continue
        a = ledger.show("ask", n)
        if a is None:
            del ask_why[n]  # a number in a workstream's free-text why that is no ask (the why is not a citation): left out, not an error
        else:
            asks[n] = a
    if errors:
        return None, errors
    parts = [INTRO] if asks or decisions else [NONE_LINE]
    parts += [render_ask(asks[n], ask_why[n], ledger.follow_ups(n)) for n in sorted(asks)]
    parts += [render_decision(decisions[n], dec_why[n]) for n in sorted(decisions)]
    body = "\n\n".join(parts) + "\n"
    ids = lambda ns: ",".join(str(n) for n in sorted(ns)) or "none"
    sha = hashlib.sha256(body.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()
    marker = "<!-- review-intent v1 asks=%s decisions=%s sha256=%s -->" % (ids(asks), ids(decisions), sha)
    return "%s\n%s\n%s%s\n" % (HEADER, marker, body, END), []


# The first line of each block pr-body-check prints for a defect in the PR's agent record (scripts/pr-body-check.ts problemBlocks; src/ledger/pr-decisions.ts for the last).
# Every other block it prints is about the description, the commits, the head or its runs: reported, not refused. test_record_heads_match_pr_body_check keeps these in step.
RECORD_HEADS = (
    "the PR has no agent record",
    "the PR's agent record has no complete principles table",
    "the PR's agent record has no Decisions line",
    "pr-decisions-check:",
)
CHECK_SECONDS = 180
LEDGER_SKIPPED = re.compile(r"^\s*decisions not checked against the ledger\b.*$", re.M)
MERGE_CHECK_SECONDS = 600  # a coordinator check-only run builds the merge result for Bookends and reads the head's runs: minutes, not seconds
RUN = {"record_check": "not-run", "merge_check": "not-run"}  # what each check did in this run; read by the log line in main()


def record_precheck(spec):
    """Runs pr-body-check on the PR's record. Returns the warnings to print; raises RecordRefused (with pr-body-check's output) on a record defect. Sets RUN["record_check"]."""
    repo, n = pr_ref(spec)
    exe = shutil.which("pr-body-check")
    if not exe:
        RUN["record_check"] = "fail-open-missing"
        return ["review-intent: warning: pr-body-check is not on PATH, so the PR's agent record was not checked"]
    try:
        p = subprocess.run([exe, repo, n, "--skip-intent-review"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=CHECK_SECONDS)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        RUN["record_check"] = "fail-open-error" if isinstance(e, OSError) else "fail-open-timeout"
        return ["review-intent: warning: pr-body-check could not run (%s), so the PR's agent record was not checked" % (e.strerror if isinstance(e, OSError) else "timed out")]
    if p.returncode not in (0, 1):
        RUN["record_check"] = "fail-open-error"
        why = (p.stderr.strip() or p.stdout.strip()).splitlines()
        return ["review-intent: warning: pr-body-check could not check %s#%s (exit %d: %s), so the PR's agent record was not checked" % (repo, n, p.returncode, why[0] if why else "no output")]
    if p.returncode == 1 and any(line.startswith(RECORD_HEADS) for line in p.stdout.splitlines()):
        RUN["record_check"] = "refused"
        raise RecordRefused(p.stdout.rstrip("\n"))
    RUN["record_check"] = "passed"
    warnings = []
    skipped = LEDGER_SKIPPED.search(p.stdout)
    if skipped:  # pr-body-check passes (or fails on something else) with the ledger comparison left out: the Decisions line was not checked against the ledger
        RUN["record_check"] = "fail-open-error"
        warnings.append("review-intent: warning: pr-body-check: %s" % skipped.group(0).strip())
    if p.returncode == 1:
        warnings.append("review-intent: note: pr-body-check also reports the following. It is not about the agent record, so the run goes on:\n%s" % p.stdout.rstrip("\n"))
    return warnings


def merge_check(spec):
    """Runs the repo's merge script in check-only mode on the PR. Returns the warnings to print; raises MergeRefused (with the script's output) when it refuses. Sets RUN["merge_check"]."""
    repo, n = pr_ref(spec)
    root = os.environ.get("REVIEW_INTENT_CHECKOUTS") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), "git")
    script = os.path.join(root, repo.split("/")[1], "scripts", "merge-pr.sh")
    if not os.path.isfile(script):
        RUN["merge_check"] = "fail-open-missing"
        return ["review-intent: warning: %s is not there, so %s#%s was not checked against the repo's merge script" % (script, repo, n)]
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(["bash", script, n, "--check-only"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=MERGE_CHECK_SECONDS,
                           env=dict(os.environ, GH_CALLER="review-intent"))
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        RUN["merge_check"] = "fail-open-error" if isinstance(e, OSError) else "fail-open-timeout"
        return ["review-intent: warning: %s --check-only could not run (%s), so %s#%s was not checked against the repo's merge script" % (script, e.strerror if isinstance(e, OSError) else "timed out", repo, n)]
    out = (p.stdout + p.stderr).rstrip("\n")
    if p.returncode == 0:
        RUN["merge_check"] = "passed"
        return []
    if p.returncode == 1 and "REFUSED" in out:
        RUN["merge_check"] = "refused"
        raise MergeRefused(out)
    RUN["merge_check"] = "fail-open-error"
    why = out.splitlines()
    return ["review-intent: warning: %s --check-only exited %d without a refusal (%s), so %s#%s was not checked against the repo's merge script" % (script, p.returncode, why[-1] if why else "no output", repo, n)]


def parse(argv):
    opts = {"pr": None, "files": [], "asks": [], "decisions": [], "state": None, "skip_record": False}
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        if a in ("-h", "--help"):
            print(__doc__.strip())
            sys.exit(0)
        if a == "--skip-record-check":
            opts["skip_record"] = True
            i += 1
            continue
        if a not in ("--pr", "--body-file", "--ask", "--decision", "--state-dir") or i + 1 >= len(argv):
            raise Usage("review-intent: unknown or incomplete option %r (see review-intent --help)" % a)
        v = argv[i + 1]
        i += 2
        if a == "--pr":
            opts["pr"] = v
        elif a == "--body-file":
            opts["files"].append(v)
        elif a == "--state-dir":
            opts["state"] = v
        else:
            if not v.isdigit():
                raise Usage("review-intent: %s takes a number, got %r" % (a, v))
            opts["asks" if a == "--ask" else "decisions"].append(int(v))
    return opts


def run(argv):
    try:
        o = parse(argv)
        if o["pr"] and not o["skip_record"]:
            for check in (record_precheck, merge_check):  # each prints its warnings before the next runs, so a refusal by the second still shows the first's
                for w in check(o["pr"]):
                    print(w, file=sys.stderr)
        elif o["pr"]:
            RUN["record_check"] = RUN["merge_check"] = "skipped-flag"
        texts = []
        linked_pr = None
        for f in o["files"]:
            try:
                with open(f, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                    texts.append(fh.read())
            except OSError as e:
                raise Usage("review-intent: cannot read %s: %s" % (f, e.strerror))
        if o["pr"]:
            text, from_record = pr_text(o["pr"])
            texts.append(text)
            if from_record:
                linked_pr = pr_ref(o["pr"])
        approvals = pr_approvals(o["pr"]) if o["pr"] else []
        ledger = Ledger(o["state"] or default_state_dir())
        linked = ledger.decisions_for_pr(*linked_pr) if linked_pr else []
        block, errors = build(texts, o["asks"], o["decisions"], ledger, approvals, linked)
    except RecordRefused as e:
        print(e, file=sys.stderr)
        print("review-intent: the PR's agent record fails pr-body-check (above). Fix the record, then build the brief; nothing was printed", file=sys.stderr)
        return 3
    except MergeRefused as e:
        print(e, file=sys.stderr)
        print("review-intent: the repo's merge script refuses this PR before the review (above, from `merge-pr.sh N --check-only`). Fix it before building the brief; nothing was printed", file=sys.stderr)
        return 3
    except Usage as e:
        print(e, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if errors:
        for e in errors:
            print("review-intent: %s" % e, file=sys.stderr)
        print("review-intent: fix the citation (or the --state-dir); nothing was printed", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    sys.stdout.write(block)
    return 0


class Tee:
    """Passes stderr through and keeps what was written, so the log can name the first line the run printed."""

    def __init__(self, real):
        self.real, self.seen = real, []

    def write(self, text):
        self.seen.append(text)
        return self.real.write(text)

    def flush(self):
        self.real.flush()

    def first_line(self):
        return next((l.strip() for l in "".join(self.seen).splitlines() if l.strip()), "")


def log_path():
    state = os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".local/state")
    return os.path.join(state, "review-intent", "log.jsonl")


def log_run(pr, code, reason, started):
    """Appends one line for this run. Never raises: a log that cannot be written must not change the exit code."""
    try:
        path = log_path()
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
        row = {"ts": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime()), "tool": "review-intent", "pr": pr or "",
               "outcome": "done" if code == 0 else "failed" if code == 2 else "refused", "exit": code, "reason": reason,
               "record_check": RUN["record_check"], "merge_check": RUN["merge_check"], "duration_ms": int((time.monotonic() - started) * 1000)}
        with open(path, "a", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(json.dumps(row) + "\n")
    except Exception:
        pass


def main(argv):
    """The one exit point of every run: runs, then logs the exit it is about to return."""
    started = time.monotonic()
    RUN["record_check"] = RUN["merge_check"] = "not-run"
    real = sys.stderr
    tee = sys.stderr = Tee(real)
    pr = next((argv[i + 1] for i, a in enumerate(argv[:-1]) if a == "--pr"), "")
    code = 2  # what an uncaught error counts as
    try:
        code = run(argv)
    except SystemExit as e:  # --help
        code = e.code if isinstance(e.code, int) else 0
    finally:
        sys.stderr = real
        log_run(pr, code, tee.first_line(), started)
    return code


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
